The remainder of this article focuses on energy and transport taxes as climate-related taxes. For an analysis of all environmental tax data collected by Eurostat (including pollution and resource taxes), see the article on Environmental tax statistics.

In 2024, corporations contributed slightly more than half (54%) of energy taxes, while households contributed 43%. Within economic producers, companies from the service sector (including wholesale and retail trade) contributed most (16% of total tax revenue), followed by companies from the manufacturing (13%) and the transportation and storage (12%) sectors. Figure 2 shows the breakdown of energy tax revenue by payer for the EU; data for individual countries can be selected via the respective drop-down option.

