In 2024, ECRs for households and all analysed economic industries reached a historic high. This is due to a combination of factors: new carbon taxes were introduced in some countries, and existing tax revenue instruments were expanded, notably the EU Emissions Trading System (EU ETS). Moreover, temporary tax relief measures which were applied in 2022 and 2023 to cushion high energy prices were gradually phased out during 2024. The rebound effect is especially clear for households.

